$ unikraft build --help

Build a Unikraft project into a container image.

Usage:
  unikraft build [<input>] [flags]

Arguments:
  [<input>]
          Path to the project directory, Kraftfile, or Dockerfile. A directory without a Kraftfile is built from its Dockerfile.
          [default: .]

Examples:
  # Build the project in the current directory
  unikraft build .

  # Build and publish an image from a Kraftfile
  unikraft build . --output my-org/my-app:latest

  # Build from a Dockerfile without a Kraftfile
  unikraft build ./Dockerfile --arch x86_64 --output my-org/my-app:latest

  # Build with custom build arguments
  unikraft build ./app --build-arg VERSION=1.2.3 --build-arg COMMIT=abc123

  # Build with secret and SSH access
  unikraft build . --secret id=npm,src=$HOME/.npmrc --ssh default=$SSH_AUTH_SOCK

  # Build for arm64 and publish the image
  unikraft build . --arch arm64 --output my-org/my-app:latest

  # Build and save to a local OCI archive
  unikraft build . --output ./dist/my-app.oci.tar

Flags:
  -o, --output
          Output destination.
      --arch
          Only build the Kraftfile targets of these architectures. Defaults to every declared target, or x86_64 when only a runtime is declared. Required when the project declares no targets and no runtime, such as a bare Dockerfile.
          [examples: x86_64, arm64]
      --build-arg
          Set build-time variables.
      --no-cache
          Do not use cache when building the image.
      --secret
          Secret to expose to the build (format: "id=mysecret[,src=/local/secret]").
      --ssh
          SSH agent socket or keys to expose to the build (format: "default|<id>[=<socket>|<key>[,<key>]]").
      --insecure
          Allow insecure (HTTP/unverified TLS) connections to registries. Specify hostnames to restrict, or omit to apply to all.
      --remote=<url> ($UNIKRAFT_BUILD_URL)
          Build on the build service at this URL and push the image from there, instead of building locally. Creates a builder with the default sizes if you have none. To set the sizes, use 'unikraft builder create'.
      --metro=<metro> ...
          Metros that a remote build may run in, by name or API URL. Defaults to the build service's choice.

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
          Path to the configuration file.
      --log-level=<level> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
          Set the logging level.
          [default: info, choices: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal]
      --log-type=<type> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
          Set the log type.
          [default: text, choices: text, json]
      --profile=<name> ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
          Set the current profile.
      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
          Toggle usage analytics.
          [default: true]
      --timeout=<duration> ($UNIKRAFT_TIMEOUT)
          Set a deadline for the command (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h).

$ unikraft builder --help

Manage the builders that remote builds run on.

Usage:
  unikraft builder <command> [flags]

Commands:
  create
          Create a builder that remote builds run on.
  get, inspect, show
          Inspect a builder.
  list, ls
          List builders.
  delete, rm, remove
          Delete a builder and its cache.
  du
          Show the disk usage of a builder's cache.
  prune
          Free a builder's cache, keeping the builder.

Fields:
  name
  default
  running
  waiting
  max-builds
  images
  instance

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
          Path to the configuration file.
      --log-level=<level> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
          Set the logging level.
          [default: info, choices: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal]
      --log-type=<type> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
          Set the log type.
          [default: text, choices: text, json]
      --profile=<name> ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
          Set the current profile.
      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
          Toggle usage analytics.
          [default: true]
      --timeout=<duration> ($UNIKRAFT_TIMEOUT)
          Set a deadline for the command (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h).

$ unikraft builder create --help

Create a builder that remote builds run on.

Usage:
  unikraft builder create [<name>] [flags]

Arguments:
  [<name>]
          Name of the builder.
          [default: default]

Examples:
  # Create the builder of remote builds
  unikraft builder create --remote https://build.example.com

Flags:
      --vcpus=<n>
          Number of vCPUs of the builder, within the range the plan allows. Defaults to the build service's.
      --memory=<size>
          Memory of the builder, within the range the plan allows. Defaults to the build service's.
      --cache=<size>
          Size of the builder's cache volume. Defaults to the build service's.
      --remote=<url> ($UNIKRAFT_BUILD_URL)
          URL of the build service that manages the builder. Defaults to the build_url of the profile.

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
          Path to the configuration file.
      --log-level=<level> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
          Set the logging level.
          [default: info, choices: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal]
      --log-type=<type> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
          Set the log type.
          [default: text, choices: text, json]
      --profile=<name> ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
          Set the current profile.
      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
          Toggle usage analytics.
          [default: true]
      --timeout=<duration> ($UNIKRAFT_TIMEOUT)
          Set a deadline for the command (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h).

$ unikraft builder get --help

Inspect a builder.

Usage:
  unikraft builder get [<target> ...] [flags]

Arguments:
  [<target> ...]
          Target builders to get.

Examples:
  # Show the builds on the builder of remote builds, and its instance
  unikraft builder get --remote https://build.example.com

Fields:
  name
  default
  running
  waiting
  max-builds
  images
  instance

Flags:
  -w, --watch=<duration>
          Watch for changes and refresh output. Defaults to 2s.
  -f, --field
          Specify which fields to include in the output.
  -o, --output
          Output format. One of: kv, table, json, yaml, raw, quiet, template.
      --remote=<url> ($UNIKRAFT_BUILD_URL)
          URL of the build service that manages the builder. Defaults to the build_url of the profile.

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
          Path to the configuration file.
      --log-level=<level> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
          Set the logging level.
          [default: info, choices: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal]
      --log-type=<type> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
          Set the log type.
          [default: text, choices: text, json]
      --profile=<name> ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
          Set the current profile.
      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
          Toggle usage analytics.
          [default: true]
      --timeout=<duration> ($UNIKRAFT_TIMEOUT)
          Set a deadline for the command (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h).

$ unikraft builder list --help

List builders.

Usage:
  unikraft builder list [<target> ...] [flags]

Arguments:
  [<target> ...]
          Target builders to list.

Examples:
  # List the builders of the build service
  unikraft builder list --remote https://build.example.com

Fields:
  name
  default
  running
  waiting
  max-builds
  images
  instance

Flags:
      --filter
          Filter output based on a field value.
          [examples: name==my-instance, metro==fra]
  -w, --watch=<duration>
          Watch for changes and refresh output. Defaults to 2s.
      --sort
          Sort output by field values. Use - prefix for descending, + for ascending.
          [examples: name, -timestamps.created-at]
      --limit
          Show at most this many builders, after filtering and sorting. 0 shows all.
  -f, --field
          Specify which fields to include in the output.
  -o, --output
          Output format. One of: kv, table, json, yaml, raw, quiet, template.
      --remote=<url> ($UNIKRAFT_BUILD_URL)
          URL of the build service that manages the builders. Defaults to the build_url of the profile.

Global flags:
  -h, --help
          Show context-sensitive help.
      --config=<file> ($UNIKRAFT_CONFIG)
          Path to the configuration file.
      --log-level=<level> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_LEVEL)
          Set the logging level.
          [default: info, choices: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal]
      --log-type=<type> ($UNIKRAFT_LOG_TYPE)
          Set the log type.
          [default: text, choices: text, json]
      --profile=<name> ($UNIKRAFT_PROFILE)
          Set the current profile.
      --[no-]telemetry ($UNIKRAFT_TELEMETRY)
          Toggle usage analytics.
          [default: true]
      --timeout=<duration> ($UNIKRAFT_TIMEOUT)
          Set a deadline for the command (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h).

